Description:
## Goal

Show a live "agent thinking" status badge in the consumer chat when a Mastra agent is executing a tool node — using `useCoAgent.running` and `nodeName` from CopilotKit v1.

---

## Why

Today the chat shows a generic spinner or no visual feedback while the agent runs. The `running` + `nodeName` fields from `useCoAgent` let us show exactly what the agent is doing: "Searching rentals…", "Routing intent…", "Fetching places…". This reduces perceived latency and gives Camila confidence the system is working.

---

## Scope

### Source pattern (from multi-agent-canvas)

```tsx
// examples/showcases/multi-agent-canvas/frontend/src/components/canvas.tsx
const { running: travelAgentRunning, name: travelAgentName, nodeName } =
  useCoAgent({ name: AvailableAgents.TRAVEL_AGENT });

// Renders: "TravelAgent agent executing search_places node"
```

### `AgentStatusBadge` component

```tsx
// src/components/copilot/agent-status-badge.tsx
interface AgentStatusBadgeProps {
  agentName: string;      // display name, e.g. "Concierge"
  running: boolean;
  nodeName?: string;      // e.g. "search_rentals"
}

export const AgentStatusBadge = ({ agentName, running, nodeName }: AgentStatusBadgeProps) => {
  if (!running) return null;
  return (
    <div className="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground animate-pulse">
      <span className="size-2 rounded-full bg-primary animate-ping" />
      <span>
        {agentName}{nodeName ? ` · ${formatNodeName(nodeName)}` : ""}
      </span>
    </div>
  );
};

// "search_rentals" → "Searching rentals"
const NODE_LABELS: Record<string, string> = {
  search_rentals: "Searching rentals",
  search_events: "Finding events",
  search_grounded_places: "Looking up places",
  route_intent: "Routing intent",
};
const formatNodeName = (n: string) => NODE_LABELS[n] ?? n.replace(/_/g, " ");
```

### Wire into consumer chat

In `src/components/copilot/copilot-kit-provider.tsx` (or the chat shell):

```tsx
const { running, nodeName } = useCoAgent({ name: AvailableAgents.CONCIERGE });

// Render above the chat input:
<AgentStatusBadge agentName="Concierge" running={running} nodeName={nodeName} />
```

If CONCIERGE-001 is merged first, consume `running` via `useAgentsContext()`.

### `prefers-reduced-motion` guard

Wrap animation classes:

```tsx
className="animate-pulse motion-reduce:animate-none"
```

---

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Badge appears when `conciergeAgent` is executing a tool (visually confirmed in dev)
- [ ] Badge disappears when agent responds (not sticky)
- [ ] `nodeName` maps to a human-readable label for the 4 active tools
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` disables animation
- [ ] No new spinner introduced — replaces any existing loading indicator in chat
- [ ] Vitest: badge renders when `running=true`, hidden when `running=false`

---

## References

* Source: `examples/showcases/multi-agent-canvas/frontend/src/components/canvas.tsx`
* CopilotKit **v1 only** — `useCoAgent` from `@copilotkit/react-core` at `1.55.2`. No v2.
* Depends on: CONCIERGE-001 (for `AvailableAgents` enum)
* DESIGN.MD: use `text-muted-foreground`, `bg-primary`, standard animation tokens — no hardcoded colors
